  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "No ‘snowflakes’: mental health review says today’s youth have it harder and harms are real",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/fonagy-review-snowflakes-young-people-mental-health",
      "description": "<p>Peter Fonagy lauds courage of young people and warns of consequences of rising prevalence of mental illness</p><ul><li><p>Full report | <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/nhs-fonagy-review-autism-adhd-mental-health-conditions-care\">NHS at risk of ‘system failures’ as demand for ADHD and autism care soars, inquiry finds</a></p></li><li><p>Explainer | <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/key-findings-fonagy-nhs-mental-health-adhd-autism\">What has the Fonagy review found and what does it recommend?</a></p></li></ul><p>Eighteen months ago, in an <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/mar/16/wes-streeting-there-is-overdiagnosis-of-mental-health-conditions\">off-the-cuff remark</a> during a discussion on disability benefit cuts, Wes Streeting said mental health conditions were being “overdiagnosed”, riding headlong into another culture war.</p><p>He later apologised for the comment, but at the time it seemed the then health secretary had endorsed a populist view that ordinary stresses and disappointments had become too often medicalised, resulting in a surge of bogus clinical diagnoses and creating a “snowflake generation” of fragile, avoidant and workshy young people.</p><p>I am in awe of their courage. Young people are contending with more powerful forces than I ever faced</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/fonagy-review-snowflakes-young-people-mental-health\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T23:01:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "NHS England mental health services review: what has it found and what does it recommend?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/key-findings-fonagy-nhs-mental-health-adhd-autism",
      "description": "<p>Prof Peter Fonagy’s 607-page report is categoric that mental distress has increased substantially and ‘cannot be explained by greater awareness alone’</p><ul><li><p>Full report | <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/nhs-fonagy-review-autism-adhd-mental-health-conditions-care\">NHS at risk of ‘system failures’ as demand for ADHD and autism care soars, inquiry finds</a></p></li><li><p>Analysis | <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/fonagy-review-snowflakes-young-people-mental-health\">No ‘snowflakes’: mental health review says today’s youth have it harder and harms are real</a></p></li></ul><p>The Fonagy review of NHS England’s mental health, ADHD and autism services was commissioned in 2025 by Wes Streeting, then the health secretary, in response to growing concerns that spiralling waiting lists for assessment, diagnosis and care threatened the NHS’s ability to meet the demand.</p><p>The 607-page report, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/nhs-fonagy-review-autism-adhd-mental-health-conditions-care\">published on Friday</a>, says that without a radical overhaul, mental health and neurodiversity services will be overwhelmed. Here are some of its key findings and recommendations.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/key-findings-fonagy-nhs-mental-health-adhd-autism\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T23:01:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "NHS at risk of ‘system failures’ as demand for ADHD and autism care soars, inquiry finds",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/nhs-fonagy-review-autism-adhd-mental-health-conditions-care",
      "description": "<p>England-focused mental health review returns stark warning and calls for shift to ‘needs-led’ system</p><ul><li><p>Explainer | <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/key-findings-fonagy-nhs-mental-health-adhd-autism\">What has the Fonagy review found and what does it recommend?</a></p></li><li><p>Analysis | <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/fonagy-review-snowflakes-young-people-mental-health\">No ‘snowflakes’: mental health review says today’s youth have it harder and harms are real</a></p></li></ul><p>The NHS in England is heading into a “world of system failures” as it struggles to cope with relentlessly rising demand for mental health, ADHD and autism care, leaving those affected desperate for support, a government-commissioned inquiry has found.</p><p>The stark warning was made in a review led by Prof Peter Fonagy into the sharp rise in demand over recent decades for help with mental health and neurodevelopmental conditions.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/09/nhs-fonagy-review-autism-adhd-mental-health-conditions-care\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T23:01:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mental health and ADHD diagnosis can cause harm, says official review",
      "link": "https://www.ft.com/content/fa7d4016-a914-4f68-97bd-82081cbde886?syn-25a6b1a6=1",
      "description": "Government-commissioned report calls for more opportunities to work and socialise for young people and rejects claims of ‘snowflake’ generation",
      "source_name": "Financial Times World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T23:01:09"
    }
